        "problem": "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9=0.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+2y)+2({z}^{2}-4z)-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2[(z-2)^{2}-4]-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2(z-2)^{2}-8-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2).$",
